WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.981
Review sheet.

2
00:00:01.261 --> 00:00:11.992
Strings are code points; UTF-8 encodes them as 1 to 4 bytes; byte-level tokenizers start from 256 tokens and can represent anything.

3
00:00:12.272 --> 00:00:26.757
BPE training merges the most frequent adjacent pair repeatedly; GPT-2 has 50,257 tokens (256 bytes, 50,000 merges, one special token).

4
00:00:27.037 --> 00:00:33.885
Encode applies merges in the order learned; decode concatenates bytes and must handle invalid UTF-8.

5
00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:40.437
Bigger vocabularies mean shorter sequences but larger embedding and output layers and rarer tokens.

6
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:48.675
GPT-2 pre-splits with a regex so merges don’t cross categories; special tokens are inserted, never merged.

7
00:00:48.955 --> 00:00:54.181
Measure tokens with each provider’s tokenizer, and route character-level work to code.

8
00:00:54.461 --> 00:01:01.053
That completes the series’ path from a derivative to a GPT; the project asks you to build and train your own.
